      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Embracing the idea that technological progress is a self-sustaining force may lead to a more pragmatic acknowledgment that policy efforts can only mitigate its effects, rather than trying to alter its trajectory. By focusing on adaptation rather than intervention, policymakers and scholars can shift their attention from trying to slow the automation wave to crafting strategies for reorienting the workforce, redistributing its benefits, and ensuring a more equitable distribution of power within society.",
